ers 27-13 on Saturday to maintain their place in the College Football Playoff hunt.","published":"2026-11-22T01:48:32.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556758/brandon-two-td-runs-lift-no-9-tennessee-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bryce Underwood makes most of second chance, sparks Michigan's upset of UCLA","description":"Reinserted as Michigan's starting quarterback earlier this week, Bryce Underwood threw a 3-yard 2-point conversion pass Jalen Hoffman, lifting the Wolverines to an 18-16 triple-overtime win over previously unbeaten No. 4 UCLA on Saturday night.","published":"2026-11-22T01:36:46.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556702/bryce-underwood-michigan-outlast-ucla-triple-over","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Nebraska's jab at Ohio State's 'THE' leads top Week 12 CFB trolls","description":"Nebraska deployed a simple but effective troll that poked fun at its opponent's propensity to emphasize the \"the\" in \"The Ohio State University.\"","published":"2026-11-22T01:12:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50554531/nebraska-ohio-state-trolls-college-football-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana's CFP hopes take hit after OT loss at Washington","description":"Indiana might not get a chance to defend its national championship after losing 27-24 at Washington on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T00:51:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556327/indiana-cfp-hopes-take-hit-ot-loss-washington","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No. 4 UCLA QB Ty Dieffenbach carted off with injury in 3OT loss to Michigan","description":"UCLA lost quarterback Ty Dieffenbach to an injury in overtime Saturday, and the Bruins ultimately fell 18-16 to Michigan in triple overtime.","published":"2026-11-22T00:49:06.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556107/ucla-qb-ty-dieffenbach-carted-3ot-loss-michigan","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 live: Tracking top moments and best highlights","description":"Tracking the top plays and developments from Week 12.","published":"2026-11-22T00:47:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50541394/week-12-live-highlights","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Preseason No. 1 Ohio State suffers fourth loss, will 'evaluate what's going on'","description":"For coach Ryan Day and his Ohio State Buckeyes, the dream of a College Football Playoff run is dead, as the preseason No. 1 team in college football lost its fourth game on Saturday afternoon, a 31-28 decision at the hands of the Nebraska Cornhuskers.","published":"2026-11-22T00:30:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50555411/preseason-no-1-ohio-state-sees-cfp-hopes-end-4th-loss","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5145410/chris-cole","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)"},"pick":{"pick":9,"round":1,"team":"TB","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Chris Cole (linebacker)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-18T13:13:47Z","intro":"Christopher Cole (born October 3, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the Georgia Bulldogs.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Cole attended Salem High School in Salem, Virginia. As a junior, he recorded 76 tackles and 11 tackles-for-loss. A four-star recruit and one of the top-rated players in the state of Virginia, Cole committed to play college football at the University of Georgia over offers from Miami, Penn State, and Tennessee."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman, Cole totaled 16 tackles and two fumble recoveries, being named to the SEC All-Freshman Team. Entering the 2025 season, he was expected to earn a bigger role in the Bulldogs defense. Cole finished the season recording 60 tackles and 4.5 sacks.Against Oklahoma in 2026, he recorded a sack and two fumble recoveries, returning one 85 yards for a touchdown in a 41–13 victory. Cole was named SEC Defensive Player of the Week for his performance. He was named a Butkus Award semifinalist in October."}]}}